Relevant columns and their possible use  
• WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES  
  – "InvoiceID": needed to link every line back to its invoice.  
  – "UnitPrice": price for 1 unit; used in the line value calculation.  
  – "Quantity": number of units sold; multiplied by "UnitPrice".  

• WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES  
  – "InvoiceID": primary key that joins to the invoice lines table.  
  – "InvoiceDate": tells when the invoice was raised; used to isolate 2013 data and to derive the calendar quarter.  

Conditions that will be useful later  
• Keep rows whose TO_DATE("InvoiceDate") falls in 2013.  
• Derive a quarter label (Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4) from the invoice date.  
• Aggregate line values to invoice totals, then averages by quarter, and finally (MAX‑MIN) of those averages.  

Below are 10 exploratory → increasingly complex Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that walk from raw data inspection to the final calculation.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes.

```sql
-- 1.  Look at a few raw invoice rows (date only)
SELECT
  "InvoiceID",
  "InvoiceDate"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Distinct years present in the invoice table
SELECT DISTINCT
  YEAR(TO_DATE("InvoiceDate")) AS "Year"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES
ORDER BY "Year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Peek at some invoice‑line records
SELECT
  "InvoiceLineID",
  "InvoiceID",
  "Quantity",
  "UnitPrice"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Join an invoice to one of its lines (first 20 matches)
SELECT
  iv."InvoiceID",
  iv."InvoiceDate",
  il."Quantity",
  il."UnitPrice"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES  iv
JOIN WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES il
  ON iv."InvoiceID" = il."InvoiceID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Add a calculated line value (= UnitPrice * Quantity)
SELECT
  il."InvoiceID",
  il."Quantity",
  il."UnitPrice",
  (il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "LineValue"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES il
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Aggregate to invoice total value (all years, 20 invoices only)
SELECT
  il."InvoiceID",
  SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "InvoiceTotal"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES il
GROUP BY il."InvoiceID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Invoice totals restricted to calendar year 2013
SELECT
  il."InvoiceID",
  SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "InvoiceTotal"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES il
JOIN WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES iv
  ON il."InvoiceID" = iv."InvoiceID"
WHERE YEAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate")) = 2013
GROUP BY il."InvoiceID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Add a derived quarter label for each invoice (2013 only)
SELECT
  iv."InvoiceID",
  TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate"), 'Q')    AS "QuarterNum",
  'Q' || TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate"), 'Q') AS "QuarterLabel",
  SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity")       AS "InvoiceTotal"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES il
JOIN WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES   iv
  ON il."InvoiceID" = iv."InvoiceID"
WHERE YEAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate")) = 2013
GROUP BY iv."InvoiceID", TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate"), 'Q')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Average invoice total per quarter (2013)
WITH invoice_totals AS (
  SELECT
    iv."InvoiceID",
    TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate"), 'Q') AS "QuarterNum",
    SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity")    AS "InvoiceTotal"
  FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES il
  JOIN WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES   iv
    ON il."InvoiceID" = iv."InvoiceID"
  WHERE YEAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate")) = 2013
  GROUP BY iv."InvoiceID", TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate"), 'Q')
)
SELECT
  'Q' || "QuarterNum"                        AS "Quarter",
  AVG("InvoiceTotal")                        AS "AvgInvoiceValue"
FROM invoice_totals
GROUP BY "QuarterNum"
ORDER BY "Quarter"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10.  Difference between the maximum and minimum of those quarterly averages
WITH invoice_totals AS (
  SELECT
    iv."InvoiceID",
    TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate"), 'Q') AS "QuarterNum",
    SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity")    AS "InvoiceTotal"
  FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES il
  JOIN WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES   iv
    ON il."InvoiceID" = iv."InvoiceID"
  WHERE YEAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate")) = 2013
  GROUP BY iv."InvoiceID", TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(iv."InvoiceDate"), 'Q')
),
quarter_avgs AS (
  SELECT
    "QuarterNum",
    AVG("InvoiceTotal") AS "AvgInv"
  FROM invoice_totals
  GROUP BY "QuarterNum"
)
SELECT
  MAX("AvgInv") - MIN("AvgInv") AS "MaxMinusMinAvgInvoiceValue_2013"
FROM quarter_avgs;
```

