Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their possible use  
• WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICELINES  
  – "InvoiceID": needed to link every line back to its invoice.  
  – "UnitPrice": price for 1 unit; used in the line value calculation.  
  – "Quantity": number of units sold; multiplied by "UnitPrice".  

• WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES  
  – "InvoiceID": primary key that joins to the invoice lines table.  
  – "InvoiceDate": tells when the invoice was raised; used to isolate 2013 data and to derive the calendar quarter.  

Conditions that will be useful later  
• Keep rows whose TO_DATE("InvoiceDate") falls in 2013.  
• Derive a quarter label (Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4) from the invoice date.  
• Aggregate line values to invoice totals, then averages by quarter, and finally (MAX‑MIN) of those averages.  

Below are 10 exploratory → increasingly complex Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that walk from raw data inspection to the final calculation.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes.

```sql
-- 1.  Look at a few raw invoice rows (date only)
SELECT
  "InvoiceID",
  "InvoiceDate"
FROM WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS.SALES_INVOICES
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Distinct years present in the invoice table
SELECT DISTINCT
